# Agent discipline

**Scope:** Do only what the user asked. No drive-by refactors, extra docs, or unrelated files.

**Code changes:** Smallest diff that solves the task. Do not rename/reformat unrelated code or delete comments the user did not ask to touch.

**Exploration:** Read targeted files first; avoid broad repo scans and huge grep dumps unless necessary. Prefer one parallel batch of reads over many sequential passes.

**Commands:** Run only commands needed to verify the change. Do not run full training or full HPC sweeps on the login node. **Never run `pytest` on the login node** — submit `bsub < hpc/submit/tests/run_pytest.sh` or ask the user to run tests on `linuxsh`. Do not run `pytest` unless the user asked or it is required to confirm a fix.

**Commits / PRs:** Only when the user explicitly asks.

**Responses:** Concise and structured; skip repeating the plan after it is done.

**When unsure:** Ask one short clarifying question instead of implementing speculative features.
